ENTRY            C2789   20260717   20261014   20261014       C259
SUBENT        C2789001   20260717   20261014   20261014       C259
BIB                 10         37
TITLE      Observation of a Near-Threshold Proton Resonance in 11B
AUTHOR     (E.Lopez-Saavedra,S.Almaraz-Calderon,B.W.Asher,
           L.T.Baby,N.Gerken,K.Hanselman,K.W.Kemper,A.N.Kuchera,
           A.B.Morelock,J.F.Perello,E.S.Temanson,A.Volya,
           I.Wiedenhover)
REFERENCE  (J,PRL,129,012502,2022)
           #doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.129.012502
INSTITUTE  (1USAFSU,1USADVD)
FACILITY   (VDGT,1USAFSU) The John D. Fox accelerator laboratory
           of Florida State University.
INC-SPECT  The primary beam of 9Be was delivered by the
           Tandem-Linac accelerator at an energy of 40.9 MeV.
           The beam bombarded a thin-window gas cell filled with
           deuterium gas at 350 Torr, which was kept at liquid
           nitrogen temperature inside the RESOLUT radioactive
           beam facility. The magnetic and electric elements of
           RESOLUT were used to select a beam of 10Be produced
           via the 9Be(d,p)10Be reaction, with a beam purity
           >= 90%, at a rate of about ~6000 particles per
           second.
DETECTOR   (IOCH,SI,TELES) The heavy reaction residues and the
           unreacted beam were detected in an ionization chamber
           placed 25.4 cm downstream from the target position,
           filled with isobutane gas at 136 Torr. The light
           charged particles were detected in a set of S1 and S2
           type double-sided silicon detectors of thickness 68 and
            1000 microm, respectively, placed in a forward dE-E
           telescope configuration at a distance of 8.6 and
           15.6 cm, respectively, from the target, covering a
           combined angular range of thetalab = 7-22 degrees.
SAMPLE     A 517 microg/cm2 thick CD2 target.
METHOD     (EDE) The secondary beam of 10Be with an energy of
           39 MeV was focused into the reaction chamber and onto
           a CD2 target. A near-threshold proton resonance in 11B
           was observed via the reaction 10Be(d,n)11B -> 10Be + p
           in inverse kinematics.
HISTORY    (20260717C) BP
ENDBIB              37
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           40
SUBENT        C2789002   20260717   20261014   20261014       C259
BIB                  5         14
REACTION  1(4-BE-10(P,0),,EN)
          2(4-BE-10(P,0),,L)
ANALYSIS   The reconstructed excitation-energy spectrum for the
           11B->10Be+p reaction main characteristic is the
           presence of a prominent peak at Eex = 11.44 +- 0.04
           MeV of excitation energy in 11B (Eres = 211(40) keV).
           The sum energy signals corresponding to the peak were
           compared to a MC simulation of the event kinematics
           based on the DWBA calculation of the (d,n)
           neutron-angular distribution for l = 0.
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) No details on sources of uncertainties.
FLAG       (1.) Tentative momentum assignment.
